# CredaFlow public demo: the two scheduled jobs (cron-run.sh). Install into
# the crontab of the user that owns the demo data dir and can run docker.
# The times assume the box clock is SAST (cron runs local time).
#
# Replace before installing:
#   <WORKTREE>  absolute path of the demo/simulator worktree (holds scripts/demo)
#   <NODE_DIR>  the directory holding node and npx, resolved once now:
#                 dirname "$(command -v node)"      # e.g. /usr/bin
#               cron's PATH does not include an nvm/fnm/volta install;
#               cron-run.sh puts DEMO_NODE_DIR first on its PATH and refuses
#               (exit 127, LAST_FAILURE) if node/npx/docker-compose are missing.
#
# Results: $DEMO_DATA_DIR/logs/ (default ~/credaflow-demo-data/logs/), and
#   <WORKTREE>/scripts/demo/status.sh
# which prints the snapshot age, image match, last bake/restore and any
# LAST_FAILURE. No notification is sent on failure: wire status.sh into a
# monitor if one is wanted.

# Nightly 02:30: restore the latest baked snapshot into the live demo stack.
30 2 * * * DEMO_NODE_DIR=<NODE_DIR> <WORKTREE>/scripts/demo/cron-run.sh restore

# First Sunday of the month 02:00: throttled bake of six months of history,
# then restore. cron ORs day-of-month with day-of-week, so the line fires on
# days 1-7 and cron-run.sh exits at once unless the day is a Sunday.
0 2 1-7 * * DEMO_NODE_DIR=<NODE_DIR> <WORKTREE>/scripts/demo/cron-run.sh bake --first-sunday
